<ProjectPage Url="/projects/mental-health-app" Kicker="Academic Project · Year 2 · COMP2912 · Software Design Brief">
                <p class="max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
                    A software design brief for a £100,000 mental health app for university students around the world. The design centers on a ChatGPT-4 Turbo companion and covers the stakeholders, the system architecture, links into university systems, crisis intervention and privacy controls.
                </p>
                <!-- Project Context & Business Requirements -->
                <ProjectSection Title="Business Context & Requirements" Icon="fas fa-briefcase">
                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line mb-6">
                        <div class="flex items-center mb-4">
                            <div class="bg-cy rounded-full w-2 h-2 mr-3"></div>
                            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100">COMP2912 Software Engineering Principles</h3>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                            The scenario: a mental health charity has £100,000 to build an app and runs a tender, with a £10,000 prize
                            for the best design. Each entry is a 6-page technical specification. The app had to support student mental
                            health at universities worldwide, with personalized AI interventions, healthy lifestyle prompts and a way
                            to handle crises.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                        <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-4">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Business Requirements</h4>
                            <ul class="text-gray-400 text-sm space-y-1">
                                <li>• £100,000 development budget</li>
                                <li>• Rollout to universities worldwide</li>
                                <li>• Competitive tender (£10,000 prize)</li>
                                <li>• 6-page design specification</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-4">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Core Focus Areas</h4>
                            <ul class="text-gray-400 text-sm space-y-1">
                                <li>• Mental health support for university students</li>
                                <li>• Personalized interventions driven by AI</li>
                                <li>• Better sleep, exercise and nutrition</li>
                                <li>• Crisis intervention and links to healthcare services</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </ProjectSection>

